{"duration_api_ms":5378,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"02f126d5-d141-4f4d-b61b-82640b0a538c","total_cost_usd":0.0006652,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":677,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":793,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":487},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":677,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":793,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":677,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":677},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1223,"outputTokens":815,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":677,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0006652,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":487,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":677,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Effect on NAV:** Trading costs reduce NAV. Commissions, the bid-ask spread paid on each trade, and market impact (price movement caused by the fund's own orders) are deducted from fund assets, so they lower the value of each share. Spreads and impact are usually the largest costs. Commissions are often small because most brokers now charge none for ETF and stock trades.\n\n**Effect on expense ratio:** Under SEC reporting rules (Form N-1A and shareholder reports), the expense ratio covers management fees, 12b-1 fees, and other operating expenses. Brokerage commissions and other portfolio transaction costs are generally excluded. Their impact appears instead in tracking difference and in returns relative to the index.\n\n**Creations and redemptions:** Authorized participants usually absorb much of the trading cost through in-kind transfers and creation/redemption fees. This limits how much the remaining shareholders bear.","ttft_ms":3495,"type":"result","duration_ms":4883,"uuid":"d2be6aa4-4c78-48ac-96ec-78b9f7ad1423","ttft_stream_ms":903,"time_to_request_ms":88,"first_content_frame_ms":903,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
